# Perturbation gate (P7 method, 2026-08-12) — PASS with documented T22 normalization

Two independent gate-vs-probed pairs (mono-inertial MH01, transition-richest mode).
Strict (from,to,reason) comparison flagged ONE systematic asymmetry:
  probed 2/2, gate 0/2: 'RECENTLY_LOST -> OK LocalMapping::InitializeIMU (cross-thread)'
Judgment: T22's from-state is declared pure-LM-timing by the golden state-trace
README ('usually lands while already OK'); its identity is occurrence. Under the
landing-state mask both pairs PASS. The systematic shift itself is recorded as
measured stamp cost: SetBadFlag stamps delay LM enough to move T22's landing
window. CONSEQUENCE: per-thread ring buffers + perturb re-pass are MANDATORY
before Optimizer-class probes (which add far more LM-thread work).

